## PROJECT OVERVIEW

JARVIS is a voice-only AI executive assistant prototype for a Mercedes-Benz CEO.
It listens for the wake word "Jarvis", processes natural language voice queries,
fetches structured data from a PostgreSQL database (or Microsoft Graph API), and
speaks the answer aloud — all within ~1.8 seconds end-to-end.

## ARCHITECTURE

```
[Android Phone]
  │
  │  Wake word: "Hey Jarvis" — Sherpa-ONNX KWS (Apache 2.0, on-device)
  ▼
[React Native App — Expo 52, RN 0.76]
  │  expo-speech (TTS) ◄────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  expo-av (STT demo cycling)                                  │
  │  react-native-background-actions (Foreground Service)        │
  │  @siteed/sherpa-onnx.rn (KWS) + react-native-audio-record   │
  │  expo-file-system (copies model assets to filesDir at boot)  │
  │                                                              │
  │  WebSocket ws://200.141.2.221:8765/ws                        │
  ▼                                                              │
[FastAPI Backend — Python 3.12, port 8765]                       │
  │  LangGraph StateGraph (classify_intent → agent → response)   │
  │  Google Gemini 2.5 Flash (free tier)                         │
  │  asyncpg (PostgreSQL connection pool)                        │
  ▼                                                              │
[PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector — Docker]                              │
  │  6 tables: people, meetings, meeting_attendees,              │
  │            action_items, relationships, meeting_chunks       │
  │  HNSW vector index (1536-dim)                                │
  │  8 C-suite seed contacts, 5 meetings, 10 action items,       │
  │  25 relationships, 20 transcript chunks                      │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

