## KEY TECHNICAL DECISIONS AND RATIONALE

### Why React Native (not web)
Android WebView does not support Web Speech API. React Native (Expo bare workflow)
gives us expo-av (audio recording), expo-speech (TTS), and access to native modules
like Porcupine and react-native-background-actions.

### Why Java is present (build-time only)
React Native compiles JavaScript to native Android Dalvik bytecode. Gradle (build
system) requires JDK 17. Java 17 (openjdk-17-jdk-headless) is installed on the VPS
as a build-time tool. It is NOT in the Docker image and NOT in runtime.

### Why port 8765 (not domain)
utilsnow.com is a personal website. Sharing it with colleagues violates privacy.
Port 8765 is open in UFW and publicly accessible via raw IP 200.141.2.221.
This is the correct URL for all colleagues.

### Why Gemini 2.5 Flash (not GPT-4 / Grok)
- Gemini 2.5 Flash: free tier, 1M tokens/day, confirmed working
- Grok (xAI): NO free tier — pay from first request
- GPT-4: paid, expensive
- Valid model names: gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.0-flash, gemini-2.5-flash-lite
- NEVER use "gemini-3.5" or "gemini-3.8" — these are hallucinations

### Why Sherpa-ONNX for wake word (Apache 2.0, no key needed)
- Porcupine required a commercial AccessKey from Picovoice (approval pending)
- Sherpa-ONNX KWS is Apache 2.0, entirely free, no account, no expiry
- Model: sherpa-onnx-kws-zipformer-gigaspeech-3.3M (~5 MB, int8 quantised)
- Keywords use BPE tokens: `▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35` and `▁HE Y ▁JA R V IS :1.5 #0.35`
- Audio capture: react-native-audio-record (MIT) at 16 kHz / mono / Int16
  emits base64 PCM chunks → decoded to Float32 [-1,1] → KWS.acceptWaveform()
- Assets bundled in APK at assets/jarvis_kws/; copied to filesDir at first launch
  (KWSHandler.kt requires absolute paths, not asset:// URIs)

### Why react-native-audio-record (not expo-av for PCM streaming)
- expo-av does not expose a real-time PCM chunk callback on Android
- react-native-audio-record wraps Android's AudioRecord API directly
- Emits base64 PCM on every ~100 ms chunk via DeviceEventEmitter 'data' event
- MIT licence, no peer deps, auto-linked via React Native 0.60+ autolink

### Why expo-file-system (for asset copy)
- Sherpa-ONNX native module opens model files with standard Java File() API
- Android assets are not accessible as filesystem paths; must be extracted first
- expo-file-system.copyAsync({ from: 'asset://jarvis_kws/...' }) handles this
- Copy is idempotent (checks existence before copying); fast on repeat launches

### Why react-native-background-actions (not other packages)
- Last release April 2026 — actively maintained
- Supports foregroundServiceType: 'microphone' (Android 12+ required)
- Alternatives (@voximplant, react-native-background-service) are unmaintained

### Boot sequence and Android 14+ restrictions
On Android 14+ (API 34), BOOT_COMPLETED receivers CANNOT directly start a
microphone foreground service (SecurityException). Our BootReceiver posts a
notification instead. When user taps it, MainActivity launches and the JS layer
(useWakeWord hook) reads WAKE_WORD_ENABLED=true from AsyncStorage and auto-starts
the service. Once running, the service survives screen lock indefinitely.

### Voice pipeline (v1 vs v2)
v1 (current):
  - STT: Demo cycling through 5 CEO queries (no native STT in managed Expo)
  - TTS: expo-speech (system TTS, free, works offline)

v2 upgrade path:
  - STT: @react-native-voice/voice (bare workflow, true live transcription)
  - TTS: Amazon Polly Neural ($16/1M chars; 1M free chars/month for 12 months on new AWS)
  - See docs/polly-upgrade.md for 7-step setup guide

### Database schema critical columns
MUST use these exact column names (mock_db.py queries are already written for them):
  - meetings.meeting_date (NOT start_time)
  - action_items.assignee_id (NOT owner_id)

### Gemini API key
Set in /root/jarvis/.env as GOOGLE_API_KEY.
Key confirmed valid: 50 models returned on API probe.
LLM-powered query types: memory, general (semantic search + LLM synthesis)
No-LLM query types: calendar_query, action_items (direct DB; no key needed)

