## DEPLOYMENT COMMANDS

```bash
# First deploy
cd /root/jarvis
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env with your GOOGLE_API_KEY
docker compose up -d --build

# Update backend code
docker compose build backend && docker compose up -d backend

# Rebuild APK after frontend changes
cd frontend/android
export ANDROID_HOME=/root/android-sdk JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17-openjdk-amd64
./gradlew assembleDebug
cp app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk /root/jarvis/dist/jarvis.apk
cp /root/jarvis/dist/jarvis.apk /var/www/jarvis/app.apk

# Check logs
docker compose logs -f backend

# Verify health
curl http://200.141.2.221:8765/health
```

## WAKE WORD SETUP (zero configuration — works out of the box)

Wake word uses Sherpa-ONNX (Apache 2.0). No account, no key, no expiry.

1. Install the APK from http://200.141.2.221:8765/apk
2. Open the app → Settings → toggle "Wake word" ON
3. Grant microphone permission when prompted
4. The notification "JARVIS is listening" appears in the notification bar
5. Say "Hey Jarvis" or "Jarvis" — app opens to Voice screen automatically

On first launch, model files (~5 MB) are copied from the APK to internal
storage. This takes ~2 seconds and is silent. Subsequent launches are instant.

Model files are in the APK at: android/app/src/main/assets/jarvis_kws/
Runtime path: /data/data/com.jarvis.ceo/files/sherpa_kws/

## MICROSOFT GRAPH INTEGRATION (v2)

Set in .env:
  USE_MOCK_DATA=false
  GRAPH_TENANT_ID=<Azure AD tenant>
  GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=<App registration client ID>
  GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=<App secret>
  GRAPH_USER_UPN=ceo@mercedes-benz.com

Required Azure AD permissions (delegated):
  Calendars.Read, Mail.Read, Tasks.ReadWrite, People.Read, User.Read

## KNOWN ISSUES AND FIXES APPLIED

1. attendees JSON string bug (FIXED): asyncpg returns json_agg as a string.
   Fixed in supervisor.py calendar_agent: parse with json.loads() before iterating.

2. llm_configured=false after key set (FIXED): docker compose restart does NOT
   reload .env. Must use: docker compose down backend && docker compose up -d backend

3. @types/react-native ~0.76.0 (FIXED): version doesn't exist on npm.
   Changed to ^0.73.0 in package.json.

4. react-native-background-actions compile error (FIXED): ServiceCompat.startForeground
   4-arg method requires androidx.core >= 1.12. Added resolutionStrategy to
   build.gradle: force 'androidx.core:core:1.13.1'

5. BootReceiver on Android 14+: Cannot start microphone service from boot.
   Workaround: show notification → user taps → app starts service from foreground.

6. Piper TTS: ARCHIVED October 2025 — do NOT use. Using expo-speech instead.

7. VPS curl not in PATH for Docker healthcheck (FIXED): Changed healthcheck from
   "curl -f http://..." to Python urllib.request.urlopen(...).

8. Porcupine commercial key (REPLACED): Picovoice AccessKey required commercial
   approval. Replaced with Sherpa-ONNX KWS (Apache 2.0) — zero configuration,
   no account, no expiry. Uses react-native-audio-record for PCM capture.

9. expo-file-system version mismatch (FIXED): expo ~52.0 requires ~18.0.x.
   Installed ~18.0.12 (not the latest 57.x which targets expo SDK 53+).

